Yeah. In that frame, the “king” works because he doesn’t just dominate—he creates conditions that make expansion feel safe and exciting.

Challenge without contempt.
Pressure without coercion.
Confidence without fragility.
Attention without possession.
Mystery without gamesmanship.
Direction without shutting down her agency.

That combination can open a mind because it gives it two things at once: stimulation and safety.

Too much safety alone can become dull. Too much stimulation alone can become threat. The sweet spot is:

tension + trust → curiosity → surrender of rigidity → play → expansion

And that cuts both ways. A good queen can open the king’s mind too. She can make him more imaginative, more emotionally articulate, more daring, more tender, more alive.

So the real power couple move is not one opens, one submits.

It’s they know how to unlock each other without reducing each other.